menu "INVOKE Band Config"

    config INVOKE_DEFAULT_BAND_NUM
        int "Default band number (1-64)"
        range 1 64
        default 1
        help
            Used only the first time a node boots with no band number yet
            saved in NVS. Set the board's real number by writing it to NVS
            (key "band" in namespace "invoke") during provisioning; this
            value is just the out-of-the-box fallback.

    config INVOKE_GATEWAY
        bool "This band is the teacher-app gateway"
        default y
        help
            The gateway band advertises connectable and does NOT scan while
            idle, so the teacher's browser connects to it reliably (a scan on
            the ESP32-C3's single radio starves inbound connection
            establishment -> reason 0x3e). It scans only once connected or
            while a round is running.

            Every other band advertises non-connectable and scans
            continuously to hear the question over extended advertising.

            With a single band, leave this on. In a classroom, flash exactly
            one band with it on (or override at runtime: NVS key "gw" = 1/0
            in namespace "invoke").

endmenu
